{# Department performance widget 'provenance' — THE derivnote.
   Design: departments/ecology/performance.widgets.js → "provenance", and the identical block at
   the foot of departments/performance.html. It is carried VERBATIM: this paragraph is the model
   canon in the user's own language, and every performance surface in the app repeats it word for
   word so the answer to "where did this number come from?" is the same wherever it is asked.

   ONE clause is data rather than prose — "Patrols is shared with Protection Service" — because on
   a department with no shared module the design's own sentence would be false. It renders the
   real shared module and the real other departments, in the design's wording, and is simply
   absent when nothing is shared. Nothing else in this paragraph varies. #}
{% set shared = department.modules|filter(m => (departmentsByModule[m.id]|default([]))|length > 1)|first %}
<div class="derivnote" data-w="provenance">
    {{ ux_icon('lucide:search') }}
    <div><b>Where these numbers come from.</b> A department has no numbers of its own. Every figure on
        this page is its <b>attached modules’ KPIs</b>, summed over the areas those modules are switched
        on in, sliced to the people whose <b>position sits in this department</b>.
        {% if shared %}
            {% set others = (departmentsByModule[shared.id]|default([]))|filter(d => d.id != department.id)|map(d => d.name)|join(', ') %}
            {{ shared.name }} is shared with {{ others }} — both read the same rows; the split is by
            recording position, not by permission.
        {% endif %}
        <b>A department still gates nothing:</b> this page reads, it never fences.</div>
</div>
